<law>
	<structure>
		<unit label="title" identifier="55.1" level="1">Property and Conveyances</unit>
		<unit label="subtitle" identifier="I" level="2">Property Conveyances</unit>
		<unit label="chapter" identifier="1" level="3">Creation and Limitation of Estates</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="4" level="4">Virginia Solar Easements Act</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>55.1-137</section_number>
	<catch_line>Creation of solar easements</catch_line>
	<text>
		Any easement obtained for the purpose of exposure of solar energy equipment, facilities, or devices shall be created in writing and shall be subject to the same conveyancing and instrument recording requirements as other easements.
	</text>
	<history>1978, c. 323, § 55-353; 2019, c. 712.</history>
</law>
